==English==

===Etymology===
Schröer suggests a combination of {{etyl|he|en}} ''mephitz'' "destroyer" + ''tophel'' "liar" (from ''tophel sheqer'', literally "falsehood plasterer, see [[שֶׁקֶר]]; compare Job xiii:4). <ref name="Englische Studien">[Eugen Kölbing].</ref>

===Proper noun===
{{wikipedia}}
'''Mephistopheles''' (or ''Mephisto'')

# The [[Devil]] to whom [[w:Faust|Faust]] sold his soul in the [[legend]].

====Derived terms====
* [[Mephistophelean]]

